.git
.gitignore
node_modules
# Not gitignore semantics: a slash-free pattern matches the context root only, so the frontend's
# own node_modules needs saying separately or the node build stage copies it in.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
__pycache__
*.pyc
.env*
.venv
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
data/
.beads/
*.md
!prompts/**/*.md
!backend/prompts/**/*.md
LICENSE
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
# The legacy data stores and exports .gitignore keeps out of the repository, at any depth, so a
# build from a working tree that still holds them cannot copy them in with backend/.
**/legacy/
**/chroma_db/
**/chroma/
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/export-*.json
**/export_*.json
**/*-export.json
**/*.dump
**/*.sql.gz
